    "name": "Siberian Kale",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Siberian kale, also known as Russian kale, is a large, hardy, biennial vegetable that's typically grown as an annual. It has flat, blue-green leaves with ruffled edges, white stems, and a mild flavor similar to cabbage. Siberian kale is high in protein and vitamins A, C, and K, and is easier to digest than other cruciferous vegetables.</span></p>",
